Here is a reproducer bash script:


{code:java}
temp_dir=3D$(mktemp -d)
cd ${temp_dir}
cat << EOF > kafka_server_jaas.conf
KafkaServer {
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 org.apache.kafka.common.security.oauthbearer.OAuthBearerLogin=
Module required unsecuredLoginStringClaim_sub=3Dprincipal;
};
EOF
podman run -it --rm \
--name kafka-sasl-broker \
=C2=A0 -p 9092:9092 \
=C2=A0 -p 9093:9093 \
=C2=A0 -v ./kafka_server_jaas.conf:/opt/kafka/config/kafka_server_jaas.conf=
:Z \
=C2=A0 -e KAFKA_CLUSTER_ID=3D$KAFKA_CLUSTER_ID \
=C2=A0 -e KAFKA_PROCESS_ROLES=3Dbroker,controller \
=C2=A0 -e KAFKA_NODE_ID=3D1 \
=C2=A0 -e KAFKA_LISTENER_SECURITY_PROTOCOL_MAP=3DSASL_PLAINTEXT:SASL_PLAINT=
EXT,INTER_BROKER:PLAINTEXT,CONTROLLER:PLAINTEXT \
=C2=A0 -e KAFKA_LISTENERS=3DSASL_PLAINTEXT://0.0.0.0:9092,INTER_BROKER://0.=
0.0.0:9093,CONTROLLER://0.0.0.0:9094 \
=C2=A0 -e KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS=3DSASL_PLAINTEXT://localhost:9092,INTE=
R_BROKER://localhost:9093 \
=C2=A0 -e KAFKA_CONTROLLER_LISTENER_NAMES=3DCONTROLLER \
=C2=A0 -e KAFKA_CONTROLLER_QUORUM_VOTERS=3D1@localhost:9094 \
=C2=A0 -e KAFKA_INTER_BROKER_LISTENER_NAME=3DINTER_BROKER \
=C2=A0 -e KAFKA_SASL_ENABLED_MECHANISMS=3DOAUTHBEARER \
=C2=A0 -e KAFKA_OPTS=3D"-Djava.security.auth.login.config=3D/opt/kafka/conf=
ig/kafka_server_jaas.conf" \
=C2=A0 apache/${1}{code}

I guess some config is needed to avoid pruning out the reflectively instant=
iated class.

`./run-oauthbearer.sh kafka-native:4.0.0` and `./run-oauthbearer.sh kafka-n=
ative:4.1.0-rc2` fail with exception.

Running the same script with the main image works:
`./run-oauthbearer.sh kafka:4.0.0` or `./run-oauthbearer.sh kafka:4.1.0-rc2=
`successfully start the broker.

For context we want to use the image for integration testing and can workar=
ound by running the non-native image if we need SASL oauthbearer.



