Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-19599) Reduce the frequency of
 ReplicaNotAvailableException thrown to clients when RLMM is not ready
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Kamal Chandraprakash created KAFKA-19599:
--------------------------------------------

             Summary: Reduce the frequency of ReplicaNotAvailableException =
thrown to clients when RLMM is not ready
                 Key: KAFKA-19599
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19599
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Task
            Reporter: Kamal Chandraprakash
            Assignee: Kamal Chandraprakash


During broker restarts, the topic-based RemoteLogMetadataManager constructs=
 the state by reading the internal {{__remote_log_metadata}} topic. When th=
e partition is not ready to perform remote storage operations, then Replica=
NotAvailableException thrown back to the consumer. The clients retries the =
request immediately.=C2=A0

This can result to lot of FetchConsumer requests on the broker and can util=
ize the request handler threads. Using CountdownLatch the frequency of Repl=
icaNotAvailableException thrown back to the clients can be reduced. This wi=
ll improve the request handler thread usage on the broker.

Reproducer:=C2=A0
1. Standalone one node cluster with LocalTieredStorage setup.=C2=A0
2. Create a topic with remote storage enabled. RF =3D 1 and partitionCount =
=3D 2
3. Produce few message and ensure that the segments are uploaded to remote =
storage.=C2=A0
4. Use console-consumer to read the produced messages from the beginning of=
 the topic.
5. Update [RemoteLogMetadataPartitionStore|https://sourcegraph.com/github.c=
om/apache/kafka/-/blob/storage/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/server/log/re=
mote/metadata/storage/RemotePartitionMetadataStore.java?L166] to micmic tha=
t the partition is not ready.
6. Replace the jar and restart the broker.=C2=A0
7. Start the console-consumer to read from the beginning of the topic.=C2=
=A0=C2=A0

~18K FetchConsumer requests per second are received on the broker for one c=
onsumer:
{code:java}
% sh kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092  --topic apple --rep=
lication-factor 1 --partitions 2 --create  --config segment.bytes=3D1048576=
 --config local.retention.ms=3D60000 --config remote.storage.enable=3Dtrue
% sh kafka-console-consumer.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic ap=
ple --from-beginning --property print.key=3Dfalse --property print.value=3D=
false
# broker logs
 % less nohup.out | grep =C2=A0"Error occurred while reading the remote dat=
a for 4ChgxqKOTPakBikyo0Thjw" =C2=A0| grep -c "2025-08-12 21:18"=20
1107088
{code}



