geric created KAFKA-19607:
-----------------------------

             Summary: MirrorMaker2 Offset Replication Issue
                 Key: KAFKA-19607
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19607
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: mirrormaker
    Affects Versions: 4.0.0
            Reporter: geric


I am using *Apache Kafka 4.0*=C2=A0with=C2=A0*MirrorMaker 2*=C2=A0to link t=
he primary cluster ({*}clusterA{*}) to the secondary cluster ({*}clusterB{*=
}).
The secondary cluster will not have any producers or consumers until a disa=
ster recovery event occurs, at which point all producers and consumers will=
 switch to it.

*Setup:*
 * Dedicated standalone MirrorMaker 2 node
 * {{IdentityReplicationPolicy}}=C2=A0(no topic renaming)
 * No clients connected to secondary cluster under normal operation

*MirrorMaker 2 config:*
=C2=A0{{# Cluster aliases
clusters =3D clusterA, clusterB

# Bootstrap servers
clusterA.bootstrap.servers =3D serverA-kafka-1:9092
clusterB.bootstrap.servers =3D serverB-kafka-1:9092

# Replication policy
replication.policy.class=3Dorg.apache.kafka.connect.mirror.IdentityReplicat=
ionPolicy

# Offset/Checkpoint sync
emit.checkpoints.enabled=3Dtrue
emit.checkpoints.interval.seconds=3D5
sync.group.offsets.enabled=3Dtrue
sync.group.offsets.interval.seconds=3D5
offset.lag.max=3D10
refresh.topics.interval.seconds=3D5}}
----
h3. Test results:
 # *Produce 300 messages when MirrorMaker is running*
*Expected:*=C2=A0Topic offset synced within a minute
*Result:*=C2=A0=E2=9C=85 Passed

 # *Consume 100 messages when MirrorMaker is running, then terminate the co=
nsumer*
*Expected:*=C2=A0Consumer offset synced
*Result:*=C2=A0=E2=9D=8C Failed =E2=80=94 offset is not synced to clusterB

 # *Restart MirrorMaker after test #2*
*Expected:*=C2=A0Consumer offset synced
*Result:*=C2=A0=E2=9C=85 Passed

 # *Repeat test #2 =E2=80=94 consume 100 messages when MirrorMaker is runni=
ng, then terminate the consumer*
*Expected:*=C2=A0Consumer offset synced
*Result:*=C2=A0=E2=9D=8C Failed =E2=80=94 offset is not synced to clusterB

 # *Restart MirrorMaker after test #4*
*Expected:*=C2=A0Consumer offset synced
*Result:*=C2=A0=E2=9D=8C Failed =E2=80=94 offset is not synced to clusterB

 # *Consume messages but keep consumer running*
*Expected:*=C2=A0Offset synced
*Result:*=C2=A0=E2=9C=85 Passed

----
h3. Problem:

Consumer offsets appear to only sync in these cases:
 # When MirrorMaker is restarted and the consumer offset does=C2=A0*not*=C2=
=A0already exist in the secondary cluster (initial sync), or
 # When the consumer is still connected at the time of sync,=C2=A0*or*=C2=
=A0when the consumer has reached the end of the offset (i.e., consumed all =
available messages).

However, if the consumer exits immediately after consuming some messages (b=
ut=C2=A0{*}before reaching the end of the topic{*}), the committed offset i=
s=C2=A0*never synced*=C2=A0to the target cluster.
----
h3. Additional Context / Related Issues

This problem seems related to an open discussion in the Apache Kafka mailin=
g list:

*MirrorCheckpointConnector does not replicate final batch of offsets*
[https://lists.apache.org/thread/dxn9jyotl00f7ov541299cd8tlcl1z00]



