Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Jun Rao created KAFKA-19634:
-------------------------------

             Summary: document the encoding of nullable struct
                 Key: KAFKA-19634
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19634
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Jun Rao


In [https://kafka.apache.org/protocol#protocol_types,] we didn't specify the encoding of a struct. In particular, how a nullable struct is represented. We should document that if a struct is nullable, the first byte indicates whether is null and the rest of the bytes are the serialization of each field.



--
