    On Friday 29 August 2025 at 11:37:24 am GMT+5:30, RShekhar Prasad <rshe=
khar.prasad@gmail.com> wrote: =20
=20
 Hello team,
While exploring Kafka Queue semantics, we released there is some APIs that =
is useful but missing for example :
1.=C2=A0 Multiple polls and ack later batch wise in explicit mode :=C2=A0

 ConsumerRecords<K, V> batch1 =3D shareConsumer.poll(Duration.ofMillis(100)=
);
 ConsumerRecords<K, V> batch2 =3D shareConsumer.poll(Duration.ofMillis(100)=
); // No IllegalStateException!
 ConsumerRecords<K, V> batch3 =3D shareConsumer.poll(Duration.ofMillis(100)=
);
=20
 // Process all batches...
 shareConsumer.acknowledgeBatch(batch1, AcknowledgeType.ACCEPT);
 shareConsumer.acknowledgeBatch(batch2, AcknowledgeType.ACCEPT);
 shareConsumer.acknowledgeBatch(batch3, AcknowledgeType.ACCEPT);
shareConsumer.commitSync(); // Commit all acknowledged batches
If we have these APIs available then multiple threads can keep polling and =
committing once their processing is done, before the timeout (and release).
In Implicit mode, we might miss(fail) the processing of the record but ACCE=
PT acknowledge in each poll(), hence that will not help in at least once se=
mantics.
2.=C2=A0 ack all API:
 shareConsumer.acknowledgeAll(AcknowledgeType.ACCEPT);=C2=A0
shareConsumer.commitSync();

Do you guys have any thought on this ?=C2=A0

Regards,
Shekhar Prasad Rajak,
